TASK: Change-aware repository sync for the scan pipeline (GitHub REST API only, runs in OCP)

GOAL
1. Skip repos whose default branch has not changed since the last SUCCESSFUL scan.
2. For changed repos, produce an exact change set (added/modified/deleted/moved files)
   and a verified workspace of the exact commit, without git or GitPython.
3. Record a repo's new state only after its scan succeeds.

RULES FOR YOU
- Do not assume anything about our environment. Every fact below marked [VERIFY]
  must be confirmed from code, config, manifests, or a live read-only API call, and
  reported with evidence (file:line, command output). If you cannot confirm one, say so.
- Do not start Phase 2 until I approve the Phase 1 report.

PHASE 1 — ANALYZE AND MEASURE (read-only)
A. Current implementation
  1. Where the zipball download happens (file:line) and every caller.
  2. How the download is pinned: commit SHA or branch name.
  3. Retry, timeout, rate-limit, and redirect handling as written.
  4. What the scanner reads from the extracted directory (full tree, or specific files)
     and the directory layout it expects.
  5. Where per-repo state (last scanned SHA, etc.) is stored today, if anywhere.
B. Environment [VERIFY]
  6. GitHub host and version (GET /meta or the /api/v3 root), and whether rate limiting
     is enabled (GET /rate_limit).
  7. Auth type: PAT or GitHub App. If App: how tokens are refreshed, given they expire in 1 hour.
  8. Proxy and CA bundle configuration used by the existing HTTP client.
  9. Pod topology: number of pods, clusters, data centres; how repos are assigned to pods;
     whether two pods can process the same repo at the same time.
 10. The ephemeral storage available to scan pods (emptyDir sizeLimit, node ephemeral storage).
C. Measurements (sample at least 200 repos, read-only API calls)
 11. Distribution (p50/p95/max) of: file count, zipball size, download time,
     extraction time.
 12. Percentage of repos whose default branch changed in the last 7 days.
 13. Repos with truncated trees, LFS (filter=lfs in .gitattributes), export-ignore
     or export-subst attributes, or submodules.
 14. Current end-to-end time per repo, split into download / extract / scan.
Deliver: a report with evidence, the list of files you plan to change, and any finding
that contradicts this spec.

PHASE 2 — IMPLEMENT
State (MongoDB, one doc per repo+branch):
  repo, branch, last_scanned_commit_sha, last_scanned_tree_sha, scan_config_hash,
  branch_etag, snapshot (gzip-compressed JSON {path: blob_sha}; store it in GridFS
  if it exceeds 15 MB), updated_at, and lease fields (lease_owner, lease_expires_at).

Flow per repo:
  1. Acquire a lease: atomic findOneAndUpdate where the lease is absent or expired;
     TTL 15 min, renewed by a heartbeat. If you cannot acquire it, skip the repo
     (another pod owns it).
  2. Resolve the default branch from GET /repos/{o}/{r} (do not hardcode main/master), then
     GET /repos/{o}/{r}/branches/{branch} with If-None-Match: branch_etag.
     If 304, or the commit SHA equals last_scanned_commit_sha AND scan_config_hash is
     unchanged, stop and report "unchanged".
     Handle these explicitly, each with its own result status: 404 (repo deleted or access lost),
     409 (empty repo), 301 (renamed/transferred: update stored name), branch missing.
  3. Fetch the tree: GET /git/trees/{tree_sha}?recursive=1. If truncated=true, walk it
     with non-recursive calls, descending only into subtrees. Keep type=="blob";
     record and skip symlinks (mode 120000) and submodules (type "commit").
  4. Diff against the stored snapshot:
       added / deleted / modified (same path, different SHA) / moved (a deleted path and
       an added path with the same SHA; with duplicate SHAs, pair deterministically by
       sorted path). No snapshot, or scan_config_hash changed -> full scope (all files).
  5. Download the zipball of the pinned commit SHA (never the branch name), streamed to an
     emptyDir. Guards: abort if size > configured max; before extracting, check total
     uncompressed size and entry count against limits and free disk space. Extract
     with the root folder stripped; reject absolute paths, "..", and symlink entries.
  6. Verify: for every tree blob, compute the git blob SHA of the local file:
     sha1(b"blob " + str(len(data)).encode() + b"\0" + data).
     Missing or mismatched -> fetch GET /git/blobs/{sha} with
     Accept: application/vnd.github.raw+json, streamed to disk, and re-verify.
     If it still mismatches (e.g. LFS pointer), record it in an "unverified" list and
     exclude it from the scan scope. Never fail silently.
  7. Return: status, commit_sha, previous_commit_sha, added, modified, deleted, moved,
     unverified, skipped_symlinks, skipped_submodules, workspace_path, reason.
  8. Expose a separate commit_scanned(result) called by the pipeline ONLY after the
     scan succeeds: conditional update (filter on the previous
     last_scanned_commit_sha) writing the new SHAs, snapshot, etag, scan_config_hash.
     If the conditional update matches nothing, log a conflict and do not overwrite.
  9. Always delete the workspace and release the lease in a finally block.

Rate limits and HTTP:
  - One shared budget per token across all pods (a Mongo-backed token bucket, or our
    existing limiter if one exists [VERIFY]). Read X-RateLimit-Remaining / Reset from
    every response and slow down before hitting zero.
  - 403/429 with Remaining=0: wait until Reset (cap is configurable). Secondary limit:
    honor Retry-After. 5xx and connection errors: exponential backoff with jitter, max 5.
  - Use conditional requests (ETag) where possible; 304s cost less rate limit.
  - Connect and read timeouts on every call; streamed downloads with a stall timeout.
  - Refresh GitHub App tokens before expiry if the auth type is App.

Configuration (env, no hardcoded values): API URL, auth, max zip size, max
uncompressed size, max entries, lease TTL, blob fetch concurrency, rate-limit caps.

Observability (Prometheus): syncs_total{status}, api_calls_total{endpoint,code},
bytes_downloaded_total, sync_duration_seconds, verify_mismatches_total{reason},
rate_limit_wait_seconds_total. One structured log line per repo with the same fields.

PHASE 3 — TESTS (required before PR)
Mock GitHub API served from a local git repo (ls-tree / cat-file / archive), plus a
real test MongoDB. Cases:
  1. First run -> full scope; workspace content == tree blobs (verify step passes).
  2. No new commit -> unchanged; 1 API call; 304 path exercised.
  3. Edit + delete + move + add -> exact change set.
  4. Scan fails after sync -> commit_scanned not called -> next run reports the same
     change set again.
  5. Two workers on the same repo -> exactly one acquires the lease; stale lease
     (expired) is taken over.
  6. Conditional commit conflict -> no overwrite, conflict logged.
  7. export-ignore file -> missing from zip, fetched via blob, verified.
  8. export-subst file -> mismatch, refetched, verified.
  9. LFS pointer / unresolvable mismatch -> in "unverified", excluded, counted.
 10. Truncated tree -> subtree walk produces the same file map as recursive.
 11. Malicious zip entries ("../x", absolute, symlink) -> rejected, nothing written
     outside the workspace.
 12. Zip over size / entry limits -> aborted before extraction, clear status.
 13. Rate limit (primary and secondary) -> waits and succeeds; budget shared across
     two simulated workers.
 14. 404 / 409 / 301 / missing branch -> correct status, no crash, state updated as specified.
 15. scan_config_hash change with no new commit -> full scope.
 16. Pod killed mid-download (simulate) -> no state written; next run is correct.
Then one run against a real test repo on our GitHub host, with results in the PR.

DELIVERABLE
One PR: the Phase 1 report, the implementation, the tests, manifest changes (emptyDir sizeLimit),
config docs, and a before/after table from the 200-repo sample: API calls, bytes
downloaded, and wall time per repo for changed and unchanged repos.
Do NOT add a persistent on-disk workspace cache. If the Phase 1 measurements show
download time is a material share of per-repo time, report the numbers and stop;
that is a separate decision.
